<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amsterdam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amsterdam is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and was the commercial and financial heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> in the seventeenth century. It hosted the headquarters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>'s largest chamber, the Amsterdam Exchange Bank and a major stock market. The city's wealth and institutions underpinned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amsterdam.jpg" alt="Amsterdam" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrés Barrios · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imagen_de_los_canales_conc%C3%A9ntricos_en_%C3%81msterdam.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
